      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "AMENDMENT TO THE SERVICE TAX ACT 2018 Commencement of amendment to the Service Tax Act 2018"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VIII__cl_52",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "52",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VIII",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Part comes into operation on the coming into operation of this Act. Amendment of section 26"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VIII__cl_53",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "53",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VIII",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Service Tax Act 2018 is amended in subsection 26(2) by substituting for the words “within thirty days from” the words “not later than the last day of the month following”."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_48",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "48",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Part comes into operation on the coming into operation of this Act. Amendment of section 26"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_49",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "49",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Sales Tax Act 2018, which is referred to as the “principal Act” in this Part, is amended in subsection 26(2) by substituting for the words “within thirty days from” the words “not later than the last day of the month following”. Amendment of section 27"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "50",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50__para_a",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50__para_b"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII",
      "schema:name": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 27 of the principal Act is amended—"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for subsection (5) the following subsection: “(5) Where any person has obtained control of any taxable goods or has imported any taxable goods, the Director General may require the person to account for the taxable goods.”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "b",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_50",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for subsection (6) the following subsection: “(6) Where any person fails to account for the taxable goods under subsection (5) by reason that— (a) the taxable goods have been sold by such person; (b) the taxable goods have been exported or removed by way of sale; or (c) the taxable goods have been lost or destroyed, the Director General may assess to the best of his judgment the amount of sales tax that would have been chargeable in respect of the taxable goods if the goods had been sold by such person and shall forthwith notify the person of the assessment in writing.”. Amendment of Schedule"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII__cl_51",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "51",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VII",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Schedule to the principal Act is amended in relation to section 25, in column (2), by substituting for paragraph 1 the following paragraph: ‘1. Substitute for subsection (1) the following subsection: “(1) The first taxable period of every taxable person shall begin from the date he should have been registered under section 13 and end on the last day of the following two months and the subsequent taxable period shall be a period of three months ending on the last day of any month of any calendar year.”.’."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VI__cl_46",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "46",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VI",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Part comes into operation on the coming into operation of this Act. New section 27a"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VI__cl_47",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "47",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_VI",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Windfall Profit Levy Act 1998 is amended by inserting after section 27 the following section: “Use of electronic service 27a. (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Director General may provide an electronic service to any registered user for— (a) the filing or furnishing of any application, return, declaration or any other document; and (b) the service of any notice, direction, order, permit, receipt or any other document. (2) Where— (a) any application, return, declaration or any other document are made and transmitted to the Director General through the electronic service; or (b) any notice, direction, order, permit, receipt or any other document is obtained by the registered user through the electronic service, the Director General shall not be liable for any loss or damage suffered by the registered user by reason of any error or omission of whatever nature or howsoever arising appearing in any application, return, declaration, notice, direction, order, permit, receipt or any other document if such error or omission occurred or arose as a result of any defect or breakdown in the electronic service or in the equipment used for the provision of the service or without the knowledge of the Director General. (3) Any application, return, declaration or any other document made and transmitted by the registered user shall be deemed to have been filed or furnished at the time the application, return, declaration or any other document is received by the Director General. (4) For the purposes of this section, “registered user” means any person who is authorized in writing by the Director General to gain access to and use the electronic service.”."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_V__cl_43",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "43",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_V",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Part comes into operation on 1 January 2025. Amendment of section 34b"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_V__cl_44",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "44",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_V",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Petroleum (Income Tax) Act 1967, which is referred to as the “principal Act” in this Part, is amended in subsection 34b(7) by substituting for the words “three days from the date” the words “seventy-two hours from the time”. Amendment of Third Schedule"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_V__cl_45",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "45",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2024/49/eng@/~part_V",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Paragraph 10 of the Third Schedule to the principal Act is amended by substituting for the proviso the following proviso: “Provided that the appellant shall give a written notice to the Special Commissioners and the Director General within a period of six months from the date the appellant receives a written notice from the Director General under subsection 46(1).”."
      }
    }
  ]
}
